break symmetry to form distinct personalities and develop complex social structures, such as consensus hubs and      
outliers, through a closed loop of behavioral inertia, metacognitive reflection, and social contrast[^2609.17331]."  

Abstract 2609.17331: "A language-model-free prototype shows the loop spontaneously breaks symmetry: initially        
identical agents consolidate distinct, stable personalities whereas matched controls do not. Experiments with a      
hosted LLM surface these differences as distinct first-person self-narratives, and a five-agent deliberation         
spontaneously develops social structure---a consensus hub and a unanimously rejected outlier---absent in the         
control."                                                                                                            

Matches perfectly.                                                                                                   

