functional specialization and higher-level self-organization without shared external objectives, though scaling these
objectives requires careful handling of failure modes that disrupt sustained exploration[^2609.17325]."              

Abstract 2609.17325: "Biological cells can be viewed as individual, interacting agents whose collective dynamics give
rise to adaptive behaviour at multiple levels of organisation... we discuss whether intrinsic rewards in artificial  
neural systems can support adaptation, functional specialisation and higher-level self-organisation without a shared 
